##CauseOfFailure=VCFv4.3.tex line 121: "All structured lines require an ID which must be unique within their type" -- both ##PEDIGREE lines have an empty ID= attribute, which VCFv4.3+ requires be present. Classified failed/ to demonstrate the CURRENT, VCFv4.3+ rule, in contrast to VCFv4.2 (see the sibling passed/pedigree-duplicate-*-id.vcf fixtures, whose grammar has no ID attribute at all).
##ExpectParser=warn
##Authority=VCFv4.3.tex line 121 (quoted above); see DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Missing or empty ID" section's eighth-type paragraph for the full construction/write-time rule this fixture exercises: at VCFv4.3+, an absent or blank ##PEDIGREE ID warns "has no ID" but is KEPT (not dropped as a duplicate), unlike the seven Map-backed keyed types.
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1), which is version-independent here (bcf_hdr_parse_line never consults ##fileformat), keeps the FIRST ##PEDIGREE=<ID=,Name_0=G0-A> declaration and drops the duplicate, exit 0, no warning -- BcftoolsDependencyTest#testPedigreeEmptyIdDuplicatesBcftoolsKeepsFirst pins this live measurement; re-confirmed directly via bcftools view -h on 2026-08-16. This library deliberately diverges from bcftools at VCFv4.3+ (keeping both, per the spec-grounded ID requirement) rather than replicating bcftools's dedupe-an-empty-ID-like-any-other-shared-value behavior -- see this fixture's other ##Authority= line and DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "The empty-ID= row is version-split" paragraph. BcftoolsDependencyTest#testPedigreeEmptyIdDuplicatesBcftoolsKeepsFirst's own probe uses ##fileformat=VCFv4.2 (bcftools's behavior doesn't depend on it, but this library's does), which is why this fixture cannot cite it as also demonstrating this library's own VCFv4.3+ behavior directly.
